      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.78,
          "end": 3.54,
          "en": "So let's build such a tasks service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.54,
          "end": 6.3,
          "en": "And for that I'll go to that tasks folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.3,
          "end": 8.61,
          "en": "though of course the position doesn't matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.61,
          "end": 11.07,
          "en": "it just should make sense logically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.07,
          "end": 13.95,
          "en": "and since it will be a service that manages tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.95,
          "end": 15.87,
          "en": "the tasks folders makes a lot of sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.87,
          "end": 17.82,
          "en": "for storing that service file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.82,
          "end": 19.77,
          "en": "So in there, in that tasks folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 24.12,
          "en": "I'll add a new tasks.service.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.12,
          "end": 27.183,
          "en": "Again following that common naming convention here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.14,
          "end": 30.69,
          "en": "In that tasks.service.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.69,
          "end": 35.69,
          "en": "we then must export a class, because services are classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.24,
          "end": 38.13,
          "en": "and it should be named like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.13,
          "end": 42.03,
          "en": "TasksService, again, following that naming convention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.03,
          "end": 44.116,
          "en": "you already know from earlier in the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.116,
          "end": 46.923,
          "en": "and also from components and directives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 51.15,
          "en": "Now, just like components and directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.15,
          "end": 54.69,
          "en": "service classes also should be decorated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.69,
          "end": 57.75,
          "en": "Though there is no service decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.75,
          "end": 58.86,
          "en": "or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 63.843,
          "en": "instead the decorator we should add here is Injectable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.06,
          "end": 68.553,
          "en": "which must be imported from Angular Core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.63,
          "end": 73.83,
          "en": "This in the end tells Angular that this class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.83,
          "end": 77.16,
          "en": "can be injected into other classes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.16,
          "end": 81.93,
          "en": "into other components, directives or services for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.93,
          "end": 84.39,
          "en": "But it's actually not just that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.39,
          "end": 86.88,
          "en": "Instead, this injectable decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 91.23,
          "en": "should also typically take a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.23,
          "end": 96.22999999999999,
          "en": "where you can and should set the providedIn property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 101.88,
          "en": "And this then could be set to any platform or root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 104.37,
          "en": "Now, I'll get back to these options a little bit later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 107.55,
          "en": "In most cases, you want root here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.55,
          "end": 109.89,
          "en": "which means that this service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.89,
          "end": 112.86,
          "en": "is set up such that it can be injected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.86,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "into any component or directive or service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 119.78999999999999,
          "en": "anywhere in your Angular application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 119.78999999999999,
          "end": 123.9,
          "en": "So no matter where you wanna use it, you can use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 123.9,
          "end": 127.233,
          "en": "and that's why this is the most common setting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 132.69,
          "en": "Now the job of this service it to manage our tasks here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.69,
          "end": 136.503,
          "en": "the tasks which we add with help of the new-task-component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.49,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "And therefor in that service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 143.37,
          "en": "we should manage a list of tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.37,
          "end": 147.48,
          "en": "and you can either manage that as an array like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.48,
          "end": 151.05,
          "en": "and then change it with some methods ends on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.05,
          "end": 153.84,
          "en": "or manage it with help of a signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.84,
          "end": 157.62,
          "en": "Both is possible, depending on the Angular version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.62,
          "end": 159.24,
          "en": "you are using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.24,
          "end": 162.957,
          "en": "Here, I'll manage my tasks with help of a signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.957,
          "end": 164.91,
          "en": "and therefor I'll create a signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.91,
          "end": 168.01,
          "en": "with the signal function provided by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.29,
          "end": 172.713,
          "en": "and I'll pass an empty array as an initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.54,
          "end": 176.61,
          "en": "Now, I also want to give TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.61,
          "end": 180.303,
          "en": "some extra information about the type of values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 180.303,
          "end": 183.24,
          "en": "that will eventually end up in that array though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.24,
          "end": 185.16,
          "en": "and that's why I'll take advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.16,
          "end": 188.85,
          "en": "of the generic nature of this signal function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.85,
          "end": 191.124,
          "en": "and add this extra type information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.124,
          "end": 194.02,
          "en": "with help of the angled brackets here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.03,
          "end": 196.71,
          "en": "and then between those angled brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.71,
          "end": 198.99,
          "en": "we define the type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.99,
          "end": 201.06,
          "en": "that will be managed by that signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.06,
          "end": 203.97,
          "en": "and here that should be an array of tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.97,
          "end": 206.7,
          "en": "and conveniently, in this starting project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.7,
          "end": 210.18,
          "en": "I already created a task model file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.18,
          "end": 213.72,
          "en": "It's this file here, which exports an interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.72,
          "end": 216.993,
          "en": "which describes the shape of such a task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.06,
          "end": 221.57999999999998,
          "en": "And it's this interface which I'm importing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.57999999999998,
          "end": 224.19,
          "en": "so that here I can tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.19,
          "end": 227.493,
          "en": "that this signal will manage an array of tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.36,
          "end": 230.97,
          "en": "An empty array, which we have initially here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 230.97,
          "end": 234.36,
          "en": "is also valid, but once we start adding items to it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 234.36,
          "end": 237.303,
          "en": "it must be items that have this task shape.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.64,
          "end": 241.47,
          "en": "So that's the first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.47,
          "end": 245.01,
          "en": "The next step is to add a addTask method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.01,
          "end": 249.24,
          "en": "which can be triggered from inside the new task component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 249.24,
          "end": 251.04,
          "en": "whenever the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.04,
          "end": 253.77,
          "en": "So whenever this method is triggered in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 253.77,
          "end": 255.693,
          "en": "in that new task component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.1,
          "end": 262.1,
          "en": "And this addTask method should then receive that task data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.59,
          "end": 265.98,
          "en": "which could be an object which has this shape,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 265.98,
          "end": 268.44,
          "en": "where have a title which is of type string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.44,
          "end": 271.803,
          "en": "and a description which is of type string let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.03,
          "end": 276.267,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could also of course accept title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.267,
          "end": 279.99,
          "en": "and description which are both of type string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.99,
          "end": 282.65999999999997,
          "en": "as separate arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 282.65999999999997,
          "end": 284.79,
          "en": "This is up to you, but here I'll got for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 284.79,
          "end": 288.903,
          "en": "a single object argument which has this shape.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 290.79,
          "end": 295.26,
          "en": "And then in here, I want to update my tasks signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 295.26,
          "end": 297.78,
          "en": "or the data managed by that signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 297.78,
          "end": 300.39,
          "en": "and we can do that with tasks.update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 300.39,
          "end": 302.58,
          "en": "a method about which you learned earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 302.58,
          "end": 303.753,
          "en": "in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 305.1,
          "end": 306.96,
          "en": "Update then takes a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 306.96,
          "end": 309.99,
          "en": "which will be executed Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 309.99,
          "end": 312.78,
          "en": "and this function will automatically receive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 312.78,
          "end": 316.11,
          "en": "the oldTasks before the update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 316.11,
          "end": 318.78,
          "en": "and then should then yield the new tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 318.78,
          "end": 320.37,
          "en": "So the new tasks array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 320.37,
          "end": 322.383,
          "en": "that should be managed by the signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 324.63,
          "end": 327.75,
          "en": "And therefor here, I'll return a new array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 327.75,
          "end": 331.14,
          "en": "where I spread my old tasks into this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.14,
          "end": 335.34000000000003,
          "en": "so I copy my oldTasks object into this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 335.34000000000003,
          "end": 339.54,
          "en": "and where I then also wanna add a new task to this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 339.54,
          "end": 341.85,
          "en": "And I'm creating such a copy here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 341.85,
          "end": 346.56,
          "en": "so that I don't mutate the old array object in memory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 346.56,
          "end": 350.013,
          "en": "but instead we replace it with a brand new object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 351.24,
          "end": 353.76,
          "en": "When working with arrays and objects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 353.76,
          "end": 358.14,
          "en": "it is typically a good idea to update data like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 358.14,
          "end": 362.52,
          "en": "where you create copies and then just change these copies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 362.52,
          "end": 365.28,
          "en": "instead of changing the original objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 365.28,
          "end": 366.693,
          "en": "or arrays in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 368.4,
          "end": 369.99,
          "en": "Now, regarding that new task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 369.99,
          "end": 372.31,
          "en": "I'll create a new object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 373.23,
          "end": 377.403,
          "en": "and I'll start by spreading my task data into this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 378.24,
          "end": 381.81,
          "en": "so this task data object which I receive as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 381.81,
          "end": 386.17,
          "en": "I spread its data, so its properties, into this new object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 387.48,
          "end": 390.19,
          "en": "and then I'll add an ID as a new property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 391.23,
          "end": 394.26,
          "en": "where I'll just create one with Math.random,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 394.26,
          "end": 395.73,
          "en": "which of course is not perfect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 395.73,
          "end": 397.773,
          "en": "but good enough for this demo app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 399.18,
          "end": 403.33,
          "en": "And I'll also set this status property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 404.73,
          "end": 406.953,
          "en": "and set this to open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 408.09000000000003,
          "end": 411.33,
          "en": "And I'll actually tell TypeScript that newTask",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 411.33,
          "end": 415.77,
          "en": "should be of type task to get extra type checking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 415.77,
          "end": 417.65999999999997,
          "en": "so that if I had a typo here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 417.65999999999997,
          "end": 419.733,
          "en": "I would get a warning from TypeScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 421.74,
          "end": 424.14,
          "en": "With that, I have such a newTask object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 424.14,
          "end": 427.503,
          "en": "and that can now be added to this tasks array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 430.68,
          "end": 432.18,
          "en": "And that is already it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 432.18,
          "end": 434.49,
          "en": "With that, I have a addTask method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 434.49,
          "end": 436.65,
          "en": "which updates this task array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 436.65,
          "end": 439.38,
          "en": "and now we can therefor call this method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 439.38,
          "end": 441.9,
          "en": "from inside the new task component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
